// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// B13. CROSS JOIN: each side still counts each of its rows once.
// Question: Over all pairs of employees, how many employees are on each side,
//   and what do they earn?
// B9 to B13 run one self-join query with each join type. e is the employee
// and m is the manager, joined on e.mgr = m.empno. KING has no manager, and 8
// employees manage nobody. The join type decides which rows reach each
// measure. No join type makes a measure count a row twice, and NULL-padded
// rows add nothing.
//
// The cross join has no condition and gives 14 x 14 = 196 rows. Each side
// still counts each employee once. A plain SUM(e.sal) gives 406350.
// Spec: 7.6, 8.1, G2 (8.3), A.6
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// KQL: CROSS pairs every employee with every employee and takes no condition; each side still counts each employee once.
FIND emp e, e CROSS emp m
FETCH agg(e.emp_count) ecount, agg(e.sum_sal) esal, agg(m.emp_count) mcount, agg(m.sum_sal) msal
